From 12312b75a1ad681a76aa814184170a9219d38d35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:34:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DIAG drm/msm: dodge first-commit trace, splash stop before
 the MDSS BCR, 1:1 splash map in the display domain

dodge_trace.c snapshots VBIF/VIG0/CTL/INTF1/DSI (clock/GDSC guarded) at
mdss reset, dpu hw init, the IOMMU attach, CTL start/flush and around DSI
cmd DMA. dodge_stop_splash() turns off INTF1 autorefresh/TE, clears VIG0
and CTL0 fetch and halts VBIF xin0/xin4 before msm_mdss_reset.
msm_kms maps the ABL splash reserved region (0xfc800000+0x2b00000)
read-only 1:1 in the display domain and keeps GEM iovas below it.

Result: the CB9 fault goes away, the -110 on the first DSI cmd DMA does
not. Not for upstream.
